{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792941978,"nonce":"+Xfi0/Qo6KX7kHxZrrGd++vhCTM=","title":"rayzor run --wasm fails to link most benchmark kernels","message":"With a freshly built runtime-wasm (cargo build --release --target wasm32-wasip1-threads), `rayzor run --wasm compiler/benchmarks/src/\u003ckernel\u003e.hx` on the NUC, at 13583a75 and with wasmtime 48.0.7 alike:\n\n- fibonacci: runs, `fib(40) = 102334155`, 2.2 s.\n- nbody, mandelbrot, and a trivial `for (i in 0...1000) s += i; trace(s)`: `wasm-linker: 1 registry-critical import(s) unresolved (haxe_type_register_to_string). The runtime-wasm artifact is older than this compiler`. The runtime-wasm was just built from the same tree, so the import is missing from runtime-wasm, not stale.\n- spectralnorm, fasta: `[wasm-linker] ERROR: signature mismatch for rayzor::haxe_bytes_free (user type 1, runtime type 0)`.\n\nThe native runtime has gained exports the wasm runtime does not mirror (type registration for toString), and haxe_bytes_free's signature differs between what the wasm backend emits and what runtime-wasm defines. CI does not run --wasm, so nothing caught it.","files":null}]}